Accepted Prototype Limitations
------------------------------
The initial prototype intentionally left several systems incomplete:

- Dream duration hardcoded to 10 seconds / 200 ticks
- Flat test Dream world
- Unsafe temporary Dream spawn
- Duplicate enter/wake logic
- In-memory-only Dream sessions
- Nested Dream sessions possible
- Beds usable inside Dream
- No vanilla sleep validation
- No activation / opt-in mechanic

Most lifecycle-related limitations were addressed during Sprint 2.



SPRINT 2 — DREAM LIFECYCLE HARDENING
====================================
STATUS: COMPLETE

Goal
----
Turn the Sprint 1 prototype into a reliable Dream lifecycle with:

- one shared entry/exit system
- persistent Dream sessions
- safe Dream entry
- correct vanilla sleep validation
- normal vanilla sleeping when Dream activation is disabled


Current Dream Flow
------------------

DREAM ACTIVATION DISABLED

Player uses bed
↓
Dream mod does nothing
↓
Vanilla Minecraft handles sleeping normally


DREAM ACTIVATION ENABLED

Player uses bed
↓
Vanilla evaluates whether sleeping is allowed
↓
If vanilla rejects sleep:
    Dream does not start

If vanilla accepts sleep:
    Player briefly enters valid vanilla sleep
    ↓
    Vanilla sleep stats / advancement behavior occurs
    ↓
    Dream mod stops normal sleep
    ↓
    DreamService.enterDream(...)
    ↓
    Player enters dream:dream


