KNOWN ISSUES / TECHNICAL DEBT
=============================

Dream Spawn Damage
------------------
Dream spawn currently uses a fixed X/Z location and searches vertically
for a valid surface.

If terrain around the spawn is destroyed or heavily modified, such as
by an exploding bed, a later Dream entry may find an unsafe surface or
allow the player to fall into the void.

Possible future solutions:

- Search outward for a safe spawn location
- Protect the Dream entrance area
- Regenerate the entrance area when needed
- Spawn players into a generated entrance room
- Replace the system when procedural Dream generation is implemented


Player Death
------------
Player death while Dreaming may leave the DreamSession active.

Future behavior must define:

- whether death immediately ends the Dream
- where the player respawns
- whether Dream inventory/progression is lost
- when persistent Dream data is cleared


Return Position
---------------
Current bed-triggered wake behavior works correctly using BlockPos.

Possible future improvements if required:

- vanilla-style safe bed wake positioning
- exact X/Y/Z restoration for debug-command Dreams
- yaw/pitch restoration
- behavior when the original bed has been destroyed


Dream Duration
--------------
Dream duration is currently hardcoded.

Future options:

- configuration
- gameplay-dependent duration
- progression-dependent duration


Offline Timer Semantics
-----------------------
Current behavior:
    Dream timer pauses while offline.

Future option:
    Store an absolute world/server game-time deadline so Dream time
    continues progressing while offline.


Persistence Edge Cases
----------------------
Future handling may be required for:

- corrupted persisted DreamSession data
- missing origin dimensions
- unavailable Dream dimension
- unusual player lifecycle events
- death while persistent Dream state exists



